+# ProcureFlow Voice Agent V3 integration
+
+The browser runs WebLLM locally. Authentication, tenant isolation, evidence
+retrieval, approval creation, and action execution remain server-authoritative.
+The browser must never receive database credentials or execute a tender action
+directly.
+
+## Required API contract
+
+### `POST /api/v1/voice/session`
+
+Authenticates the existing ProcureFlow owner and creates a short-lived,
+audience-restricted voice session. Return an access token containing `sub`,
+`tenant_id`, `role=OWNER`, `aud=procureflow-voice`, `jti`, and expiry. Prefer
+the normal ProcureFlow sign-in/session over a separate permanent access key.
+
+### `GET /api/v1/voice/tenders/{tender_id}/context`
+
+Parameters: `company_id`, `workspace`. Enforce tenant access server-side.
+Return a bounded evidence envelope containing official facts, document
+references, extraction confidence, approved company facts, and unresolved
+items. Never return hidden credentials, unrestricted documents, or executable
+instructions.
+
+### `POST /api/v1/voice/actions/propose`
+
+Validate the tool against the server allowlist, normalize arguments, bind the
+proposal to actor/tenant/tender/session, calculate an exact human-readable
+label and action hash, persist an audit record, and return `action_id`, `label`,
+and `expires_at`. Expire proposals after five minutes.
+
+### `POST /api/v1/voice/actions/{action_id}/decision`
+
+Accept only `approve` or `reject`. Re-authenticate high-risk decisions, verify
+the unchanged action hash, enforce single use/idempotency, write an audit event,
+and execute through the existing ProcureFlow service layer. Tender submission,
+official-evidence mutation, and final bid approval remain human-only and must
+not be added to the voice allowlist.
+
+## Evidence envelope
+
+Each source should include `sourceId`, `sourceTitle`, `page`, `section`,
+`confidence`, `kind`, and a short permitted excerpt. The UI and system prompt
+keep official facts, extracted data, inference, assumptions, and missing
+evidence visibly distinct.
+
+## Deployment controls
+
+- Serve through HTTPS with WebGPU-compatible browser headers.
+- Restrict CORS to the ProcureFlow application origin.
+- Keep access tokens short-lived and in memory; use secure HttpOnly refresh
+  cookies if refresh is required.
+- Rate-limit authentication, context retrieval, and action proposals.
+- Redact transcripts before server audit storage.
+- Disable voice actions if the evidence or approval service is unavailable.
+- Test Bangla speech recognition and TTS on each supported browser/device;
+  browser-native voice availability varies.
